BioRouter modifications are recorded in patches/ and the shipped manifest.
The upstream extracted cursor artwork is not distributed. The BioRouter cursor
is an original procedurally drawn blue pointer generated by our build script.
Upstream's optional WebP encoder (libwebp) is not built into this helper.
Linux requires distro Python, PyGObject, AT-SPI2 and GTK3 (declared package deps).

Upstream's THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md names code it derives from the projects below.
Their licences follow.

Cua Driver
https://github.com/trycua/cua (revision b8a0f32a06c75225ba24ebb5ab14f6507fa90d15)
Used by upstream for the macOS SkyLight event bridge and target-only activation
record. BioRouter's helper refuses sky_click and sky_key input.

